<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="029" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>External To Do read + create parity with PATCH -- matter and work assignment, per the owner's regarding decision</title>
    <phase>0 Enforcement Remediation</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs on the external-access read AND write path; adds a Dataverse write shape (new @odata.bind nav props) and changes a client-visible contract.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The pattern exists twice already -- the documents module's OR'd ScopeDimension list for the read half, and CreateTodoAsync's own project path for the write half. This is a third instance, not a new mechanism.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs, Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs and Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs -- all contended external-access paths.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>009</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, dataverse, security</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Filed 2026-08-24 by owner decision, from the task-009 read/write asymmetry. Task 009 widened PATCH /todos/{id} to matter and work assignment per the owner's ruling that "matter and work assignment should have same functionality as project"; the read and create paths were left project-only, so PATCH is now WIDER than list. The owner also stated the product intent directly: a To Do must be associable to ANY regarding entity, and the parent must flow from the creation context (create a To Do while on a Matter -> sprk_regardingmatter plus the four resolver fields).</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Task 009 widened the external To Do PATCH to matter- and work-assignment-parented to-dos per the owner's parity decision, but left GetTodosAsync and CreateTodoAsync project-only. The write plane is therefore wider than the read plane: a caller can PATCH a matter-parented to-do the same plane will not list and cannot create. Close the asymmetry in the direction the owner specified -- read and create reach matter and work assignment too, with the parent flowing from creation context and the four ADR-024 resolver fields stamped for whichever parent type it is.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the external-access data plane (ExternalDataService, ExternalModuleRegistry ScopeDimension scoping, Tier2ScopeFilterInjector) and ADR-024 multi-entity regarding on sprk_todo.</role>

  <goal>The external To Do surface is symmetric across read, create and update for all three A-9 accessible roots: a caller who can PATCH a matter-parented to-do can also list and create matter-parented to-dos, and no caller can read or create outside their accessible sets. The four ADR-024 resolver fields are stamped correctly for whichever parent type the create names.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 009 (commits b8414aeb3, 9294f0182) added GetTodoRootAsync + a root-scoped gate to PATCH /api/v1/external/todos/{id}, covering project, matter and work assignment. GetTodosAsync still filters on `_sprk_regardingproject_value eq {projectId}` only, and CreateTodoAsync still hard-codes the project parent. The result is a real asymmetry, not a cosmetic one: the SPA cannot show or create the very records it is now allowed to edit.

The owner's product intent (stated 2026-08-24): "To Do need to be able to be associated to any of the 'regarding' entities; this should flow when the To Do was created 'from' or in context of its parent (e.g., if I'm on a Matter, and 'Create To Do', the matter is set as the To Do's sprk_regardingmatter and sprk_regardingrecord, sprk_regardingrecordnumber, sprk_regardingrecordtype etc.)". The authorization boundary of THIS project caps that at the three roots that have accessible sets; service request is task 028, and the remaining nine regarding types have no accessible set at all (see the GetTodoRootAsync remarks).

TWO EXISTING MECHANISMS ALREADY DO MOST OF THIS -- find them before writing anything new (CLAUDE.md §11):

(1) READ. `ExternalAccessModule.cs:189-195` registers the `documents` external module with exactly the OR'd three-dimension scope this needs:
      new ScopeDimension { Attribute = "sprk_project",        AccessibleIds = p =&gt; p.GetAccessibleProjectIds().ToHashSet() },
      new ScopeDimension { Attribute = "sprk_matter",         AccessibleIds = p =&gt; p.GetAccessibleMatterIds() },
      new ScopeDimension { Attribute = "sprk_workassignment", AccessibleIds = p =&gt; p.GetAccessibleWorkAssignmentIds() },
    `invoices` declares a two-dimension version. There is NO `todos` module. Decide deliberately whether the To Do read belongs on the generic scoped-fetch plane (`POST /api/v1/external/data/fetch` + Tier2ScopeFilterInjector) as a registered module, or on bespoke sibling routes -- and say why. A registered module is the reuse answer; bespoke routes are justified only if the SPA's To Do view genuinely cannot consume the generic plane. Note the attribute names in that list are LOOKUP names, not the `_value` forms, and sprk_todo's lookups are `sprk_regardingproject` / `sprk_regardingmatter` / `sprk_regardingworkassignment` -- verify against live metadata, do not pattern-match.

(2) CREATE. `ExternalDataService.ApplyResolverFieldsAsync` (private, ~line 528) is ALREADY generic in the entity name: it takes `regardingEntityName`, stamps sprk_regardingrecordid / name / url, and resolves `sprk_RegardingRecordType@odata.bind` dynamically through `ResolveRecordTypeRefAsync` against `sprk_recordtype_ref`. So the resolver-field half of the owner's ask needs NO new code. Exactly two things in `CreateTodoAsync` are hard-coded to project: the specific lookup bind `body["sprk_RegardingProject@odata.bind"] = $"/sprk_projects({projectId})"`, and the `GetProjectByIdAsync` call that supplies the display name. Those two are the whole write-side change.

Also read `Services/Workspace/TodoRegardingBuilder.cs` -- its `RegardingLookupByEntity` map already enumerates every supported sprk_todo regarding parent on the SDK path, and it enforces the ADR-024 one-parent-at-a-time rule. It is the authority for which ATTRIBUTE belongs to which entity. It is NOT the authority for the `@odata.bind` navigation-property casing, which is a different name and must come from $metadata.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleRegistry.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Workspace/TodoRegardingBuilder.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalTodoScopeTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/unified-access-control-r2/spec.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">PERTURBATION IS MANDATORY. After the fix, break it one line at a time and record how many tests fail. A perturbation that fails ZERO means the test is at the wrong level -- fix the test, never drop the perturbation. Task 009 hit this TWICE in this exact file pair: once because two guards denied the same case so a status-code assertion could not tell them apart (fixed by asserting WHICH guard denied, via the response detail), and once because a new membership check had a positive test and no negative one (fixed by adding the negative). Pair every positive with a negative, and assert the distinguishing observable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">VERIFY EVERY COLUMN AND NAVIGATION PROPERTY against live Dataverse metadata (Dataverse MCP describe / $metadata) before writing any $select, $filter, $orderby or @odata.bind. SIX stale-column instances have been found in this project; the sixth (H5, task 022) was an $orderby on `sprk_name` sitting one line BELOW a correct $select -- so check every clause that names a column, not just the select. An @odata.bind navigation property is case-sensitive PascalCase and is NOT derivable from the attribute name: `sprk_regardingproject` binds as `sprk_RegardingProject`, and matter / work assignment may not follow the same capitalization. Get all three from metadata.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">DIFFERENT FAILURE MODE FROM TASK 021 -- do not carry 021's fear across without checking. CreateTodoAsync THROWS on any non-success response, so a wrong @odata.bind name fails loudly with a 400 rather than being silently swallowed (021's provisioning PATCH swallowed its 400, which is why wrong names there were invisible). Get the names from metadata anyway; but if a name is wrong here you will see it, so do not add a defensive swallow "to be safe" -- that would manufacture 021's bug in a file that does not have it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Reuse before you build. The `documents` module entry is a working three-dimension scope declaration and `ApplyResolverFieldsAsync` is already entity-generic. If you end up adding a new service, a new interface, or a second copy of the entity-to-lookup mapping, stop and justify it against those two -- a second mapping table is exactly how an attribute-name transposition gets introduced (this project already has the AppendAccess/AppendToAccess precedent).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">At most ONE specific regarding lookup may be set on a to-do. The four resolver fields (sprk_regardingrecordid, sprk_regardingrecordname, sprk_regardingrecordurl, sprk_RegardingRecordType) are written ATOMICALLY with the lookup in the same request -- never in a follow-up PATCH. TodoRegardingBuilder enforces the one-parent rule on the SDK path; the Web API path must not be able to create a two-parent row that GetTodoRootAsync would then classify as Ambiguous and deny forever.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed on BOTH new paths. A create naming a parent outside the caller's accessible set must deny before any Dataverse write. A list for a root outside the accessible set must deny, not return an empty collection -- an empty list is indistinguishable from "no to-dos" and hides the denial.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">THE LEVEL ASYMMETRY IS LOAD-BEARING HERE -- decide it explicitly and write the decision down. `CreateTodo` today requires `AccessRights.Create` from `GetEffectiveRights(projectId)`. Project access carries a level (ExternalAccessLevel -> AccessRights); the matter and work-assignment accessible sets are bare IReadOnlySet&lt;Guid&gt; with NO level anywhere in the pipeline, so membership would imply create. That is the same asymmetry task 009 accepted for PATCH, and it is owner-approved for update -- but CREATE is a different act. Either follow 009's precedent (membership implies create; say so in a comment) or block create on the levelless roots. Do not leave it implicit either way, and record the reasoning in the notes file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests go on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,regression,data-mutation,tenant,contract,seam}/** or tests/unit/domain/**). Extend the EXISTING tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalTodoScopeTests.cs and its ExternalTodoScopeTestFixture -- they already substitute ICallerPrincipalResolver and a StubExternalDataService subclass, and the fixture's load-bearing assertion is a call-count, not a status code. Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; stays banned (B1), as do DI-registration tests (B3), ctor null-checks (B4), reflection into privates (B8) and coverage-fillers (B10).</constraint>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">Mocking at a seam proves the CALLER, never the CALLEE. If you widen GetTodosAsync's $filter, a test that substitutes GetTodosAsync cannot see the filter -- assert the emitted OData at the level that actually builds it, or the widening ships untested. Task 017 shipped an untested fix in this exact shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF-touching task (CLAUDE.md §10): state the Placement Justification in the PR citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md, and report publish size vs the 43.70 MB baseline; ceiling 60 MB compressed incl. PDBs. Run /conflict-check before the PR -- this surface is shared with SPA-external-access-platform-r1/r2 and teams-app-r1 (shipped) and SPA-r3 (draft).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">CLIENT CONTRACT. Adding routes or a module changes what the external SPA can call. Do NOT change or remove the existing project-scoped routes' shapes -- SPA-r1/r2 are shipped against them. New capability is additive. If the read half lands as a registered module rather than routes, note in the PR that the SPA needs a corresponding client change and that this task does not deliver it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

