  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>All three @odata.bind navigation properties and all three lookup attribute names are recorded in the notes file with live metadata as their cited source.</criterion>
    <criterion>The read-half placement decision (registered module vs sibling routes) is written down with its reason before the implementation, and the chosen shape reuses the existing mechanism rather than duplicating it.</criterion>
    <criterion>A caller holding a matter can list to-dos parented to that matter; a caller who does not hold it cannot, and the denial is a denial -- not an empty collection.</criterion>
    <criterion>The same holds for work assignment, and the existing project behaviour is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion>A create naming a matter or work-assignment parent stamps the specific lookup plus all four ADR-024 resolver fields atomically, with the resolver fields carrying the PARENT's entity (not sprk_project).</criterion>
    <criterion>A create naming a parent outside the caller's accessible set denies with no Dataverse write -- proven by call count, not by status code alone.</criterion>
    <criterion>A create that would set more than one regarding lookup is rejected.</criterion>
    <criterion>The create-side level decision is implemented, commented at the decision site, and its reasoning recorded in the notes file.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every one of the five perturbations in step 6 fails at least one test; counts recorded in the notes file.</criterion>
    <criterion>FR-08's acceptance criteria in spec.md name read, create AND update parity across the three roots.</criterion>
    <criterion>The notes file states explicitly which parts of the owner's "any regarding entity" intent remain unimplemented (service request; the nine levelless regarding types) and what each needs.</criterion>
    <criterion>All 7 test projects pass; publish size reported and &lt;=60 MB compressed incl. PDBs.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Filed 2026-08-24 by owner decision from the task-009 asymmetry. Read notes/task-009-external-todo-scope.md first -- it records the level asymmetry, the two zero-failure perturbations this file pair produced, and the GetTodoRootAsync fail-closed contract. Task 028 (service request accessible set) is the natural follow-on for the fourth root; do not fold it in here.</notes>
</task>
